ate of expansion is $\\text{div}\\,V\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366286 1113 #uuid "bf64bea8-4a99-5229-a780-9901d768c296" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366286 1145 "If $V=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $V$ all exist, then the divergence of $V$ is given by\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot V=\\text{div}\\,V=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,V & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy) \\\\  & =2xy+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,V$ at the point $(1,1),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,V\\,{|}_{(1,\\,1)} & =2(1)(1)+2(1) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186366288 13194139535788 true] [17592186366287 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535788 true] [17592186366287 1041 "field-1" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366287 1104 #edb/ref 17592186366288 13194139535788 true] [17592186366287 1110 #uuid "b0d1ea9c-980b-527d-b61b-7353047aa563" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366288 1034 "4" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535788 true] [17592186366288 1111 #uuid "60e6a797-efa3-54b9-9b99-78bb01350914" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366289 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366290 13194139535788 true] [17592186366289 1017 #edb/ref 17592186366292 13194139535788 true] [17592186366289 1089 "q-168114" 13194139535788 true] [17592186366289 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535788 true] [17592186366289 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069903/assets/4fce9c5eebc7b439d9851ed0ed20df2e0879161b754d63fcd31502b26a8fb82e.png)\n\n \n\nA thin 